module

public import StacksFrontier.Homology.TwoTermComplex.DeterminantLineHomBaseChange

/-!
# Transitivity of the base-change comparison for determinant lines

Let `R → A → B` be a tower of commutative rings and let `M` be a finite projective `R`-module.
Base change along `R → B` can be performed in one step or in two, and the two results are
identified by `TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange`:
`B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M) ≅ B ⊗_R M`. This file proves that the comparison
`ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv` of the determinant line with base change is compatible
with that identification: performing base change in two steps and then cancelling agrees with
performing it in one step. The same statement is then deduced for the determinant line
`TwoTermComplex.determinantLine` of a two-term complex.

The content is the corresponding statement for exterior algebras, which is proved by exhibiting
the two comparisons as `R`-algebra maps out of `⋀_R M` and comparing them on the degree-one
generators.

## Main results

* `ProjectiveDeterminant.exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_comp`: **the two-step comparison of exterior
  algebras agrees with the one-step comparison**, after the identification
  `B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M) ≅ B ⊗_R M` of the underlying modules.
* `ProjectiveDeterminant.exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_comp`: the same square read in the
  direction of the inverses, which is the direction the proof runs in.
* `ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv_comp`: **the two-step base change of the determinant
  line agrees with the one-step base change.**
* `ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv_comp_tmul`: the same on a general pure tensor.
* `TwoTermComplex.determinantLineBaseChange_comp`: **the comparison of determinant lines of a
  two-term complex is transitive** along a tower of flat ring maps.

## Implementation notes

The square of exterior algebras is proved in the direction of the *inverses* of the three
comparisons. That direction starts at `B ⊗_R ⋀_R M`, which is a tensor product, so
`TensorProduct.inductionOn` applies; `B`-semilinearity then reduces matters to the pure tensors
`1 ⊗ₜ w`. On those, both composites are `R`-algebra maps out of `⋀_R M` — the inverses of the
comparisons are algebra equivalences, `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight` is an algebra map, and
`ExteriorAlgebra.map` of a linear map is an algebra map, all put over `R` by
`AlgHom.restrictScalars` — so `ExteriorAlgebra.hom_ext` reduces the identity to the degree-one
generators `ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m`, where `ProjectiveDeterminant.exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_ι` and
`TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange_symm_tmul` finish it. A direct attack on the
stated direction is not available: its source `⋀_B (B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M))` is neither a tensor product
nor an algebra generated by elements the comparisons are specified on.

The statement for a two-term complex is reduced to the statement for a single module by
`TwoTermComplex.determinantLineBaseChange_one_tmul`, which writes the comparison as conjugation
by `ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv`; the two nested inductions appearing there are over
the two tensor products `B ⊗_A det(A ⊗_R K₁)` and `A ⊗_R det(K₁)`, reached by surjectivity of
the two comparisons.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FJA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FJA)
* [Stacks Project, Section 15.124 (Tag 0FJI)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FJI)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 36.39.1 (Tag 0FJX)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FJX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open scoped TensorProduct

open TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule (cancelBaseChange)

namespace ProjectiveDeterminant

universe u

section ExteriorAlgebraMap

variable {S : Type*} [CommRing S] {N P : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module S N]
  [AddCommGroup P] [Module S P]

/-- The exterior-algebra maps induced by a linear equivalence and by its inverse are mutually
inverse. -/
theorem exteriorAlgebra_map_comp_map_symm (e : N ≃ₗ[S] P) :
    (ExteriorAlgebra.map e.toLinearMap).comp (ExteriorAlgebra.map e.symm.toLinearMap) =
      AlgHom.id S (ExteriorAlgebra S P) := by
  have h : e.toLinearMap ∘ₗ e.symm.toLinearMap = LinearMap.id := by ext v; simp
  rw [ExteriorAlgebra.map_comp_map, h, ExteriorAlgebra.map_id]

/-- The exterior-algebra maps induced by a linear equivalence and by its inverse are mutually
inverse, composed in the other order. -/
theorem exteriorAlgebra_map_symm_comp_map (e : N ≃ₗ[S] P) :
    (ExteriorAlgebra.map e.symm.toLinearMap).comp (ExteriorAlgebra.map e.toLinearMap) =
      AlgHom.id S (ExteriorAlgebra S N) := by
  have h : e.symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ e.toLinearMap = LinearMap.id := by ext v; simp
  rw [ExteriorAlgebra.map_comp_map, h, ExteriorAlgebra.map_id]

end ExteriorAlgebraMap

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
  (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra R B] [IsScalarTower R A B]
  (M : Type u) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-! ### Transitivity for exterior algebras -/

/-- **The two-step and the one-step base-change comparisons of exterior algebras agree on the
pure tensors `1 ⊗ₜ w`**, read through the inverses of the comparisons.

This is the heart of the matter. Both sides are the values at `w` of `R`-algebra maps out of
`⋀_R M`, so `ExteriorAlgebra.hom_ext` reduces the identity to the degree-one generators, where
both sides are `ι_B (1 ⊗ₜ 1 ⊗ₜ m)`. -/
theorem exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_one_tmul_one_tmul (w : ExteriorAlgebra R M) :
    (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange A B (A ⊗[R] M)).symm
        ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R A M).symm ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] w)) =
      ExteriorAlgebra.map (cancelBaseChange R A B B M).symm.toLinearMap
        ((exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R B M).symm ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[R] w)) := by
  have h := map_cancelBaseChange_exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm A B M 1 1 w
  rw [one_smul] at h
  rw [← h, ← AlgHom.comp_apply, exteriorAlgebra_map_symm_comp_map, AlgHom.id_apply]

/-- `ProjectiveDeterminant.exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_one_tmul_one_tmul` with the
identification `B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M) ≅ B ⊗_R M` moved to the other side. -/
theorem map_exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_one_tmul_one_tmul (w : ExteriorAlgebra R M) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.map (cancelBaseChange R A B B M).toLinearMap
      ((exteriorAlgebraBaseChange A B (A ⊗[R] M)).symm
        ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R A M).symm ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] w))) =
      (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R B M).symm ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[R] w) := by
  rw [exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_one_tmul_one_tmul R A B M w, ← AlgHom.comp_apply,
    exteriorAlgebra_map_comp_map_symm, AlgHom.id_apply]

/-- **The square comparing the two-step and the one-step base change of the exterior algebra
commutes**, read in the direction of the inverses of the three comparisons:
```
  B ⊗_R ⋀_R M ---> B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R ⋀_R M) ---> B ⊗_A ⋀_A (A ⊗_R M) ---> ⋀_B (B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M))
       |                                                                       ‖
  ⋀_B (B ⊗_R M) --------------------------------------------------->  ⋀_B (B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M))
```
This is the direction the proof runs in: the source is a tensor product, so
`TensorProduct.inductionOn` and `B`-semilinearity reduce the statement to
`ProjectiveDeterminant.exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_one_tmul_one_tmul`. -/
theorem exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_comp :
    (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange A B (A ⊗[R] M)).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.congr (LinearEquiv.refl B B)
          (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R A M).toLinearEquiv).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (cancelBaseChange R A B B (ExteriorAlgebra R M)).symm.toLinearMap =
      (ExteriorAlgebra.map (cancelBaseChange R A B B M).symm.toLinearMap).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R B M).symm.toLinearMap := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun v => ?_
  induction v using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add v w hv hw => simp only [map_add, hv, hw]
  | tmul b w =>
      have hb : (b : B) ⊗ₜ[R] w = b • ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[R] w) :=
        TensorProduct.tmul_eq_smul_one_tmul b w
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply,
        AlgEquiv.toLinearMap_apply, hb, map_smul,
        TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange_symm_tmul,
        TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.congr_symm_tmul, LinearEquiv.refl_symm,
        LinearEquiv.refl_apply, ← AlgEquiv.toLinearEquiv_symm, AlgEquiv.coe_toLinearEquiv]
      rw [exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_one_tmul_one_tmul R A B M w]

/-- **The square comparing the two-step and the one-step base change of the exterior algebra
commutes**:
```
  ⋀_B (B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M)) ---> B ⊗_A ⋀_A (A ⊗_R M) ---> B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R ⋀_R M) ---> B ⊗_R ⋀_R M
            |                                                                        ‖
  ⋀_B (B ⊗_R M) ---------------------------------------------------------->  B ⊗_R ⋀_R M
```
the left vertical arrow being `ExteriorAlgebra.map` of the cancellation
`B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M) ≅ B ⊗_R M`. This is
`ProjectiveDeterminant.exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_comp` with every arrow inverted. -/
theorem exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_comp :
    (cancelBaseChange R A B B (ExteriorAlgebra R M)).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.congr (LinearEquiv.refl B B)
          (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R A M).toLinearEquiv).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange A B (A ⊗[R] M)).toLinearMap =
      (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R B M).toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        (ExteriorAlgebra.map (cancelBaseChange R A B B M).toLinearMap).toLinearMap := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun y => ?_
  have hy : ExteriorAlgebra.map (cancelBaseChange R A B B M).symm.toLinearMap
      (ExteriorAlgebra.map (cancelBaseChange R A B B M).toLinearMap y) = y := by
    rw [← AlgHom.comp_apply, exteriorAlgebra_map_symm_comp_map, AlgHom.id_apply]
  have h := LinearMap.congr_fun (exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_comp R A B M)
    ((exteriorAlgebraBaseChange R B M)
      (ExteriorAlgebra.map (cancelBaseChange R A B B M).toLinearMap y))
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply,
    AlgEquiv.toLinearMap_apply, AlgEquiv.symm_apply_apply, hy] at h
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply,
    AlgEquiv.toLinearMap_apply]
  conv_lhs => rw [← h]
  simp

/-! ### Transitivity for the determinant line of a module -/

variable [Module.Finite R M] [Module.Projective R M]

/-- **The base change of the determinant line is transitive.** Base changing `det(M)` from `R`
to `A` and then to `B`, and identifying `B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R M)` with `B ⊗_R M`, gives the base change
of `det(M)` from `R` to `B`.

Pushed into the exterior algebra by `ProjectiveDeterminant.coe_baseChangeEquiv_tmul`, this is
`ProjectiveDeterminant.map_exteriorAlgebraBaseChange_symm_one_tmul_one_tmul`. -/
theorem baseChangeEquiv_comp (x : module (R := R) (M := M)) :
    mapEquiv (cancelBaseChange R A B B M)
        (baseChangeEquiv (R := A) (A := B) (M := A ⊗[R] M)
          ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] baseChangeEquiv (R := R) (A := A) (M := M) ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] x))) =
      baseChangeEquiv (R := R) (A := B) (M := M) ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[R] x) := by
  simpa using mapEquiv_cancelBaseChange_baseChangeEquiv_tmul A B (M := M) 1 1 x

/-- `ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv_comp` on a general pure tensor: the two scalars are
multiplied into one by the cancellation `B ⊗_A A ≅ B`. -/
theorem baseChangeEquiv_comp_tmul (b : B) (a : A) (x : module (R := R) (M := M)) :
    mapEquiv (cancelBaseChange R A B B M)
        (baseChangeEquiv (R := A) (A := B) (M := A ⊗[R] M)
          (b ⊗ₜ[A] baseChangeEquiv (R := R) (A := A) (M := M) (a ⊗ₜ[R] x))) =
      baseChangeEquiv (R := R) (A := B) (M := M) ((a • b) ⊗ₜ[R] x) := by
  exact mapEquiv_cancelBaseChange_baseChangeEquiv_tmul A B a b x

end ProjectiveDeterminant

/-! ### Transitivity for the determinant line of a two-term complex -/

namespace TwoTermComplex

universe u

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]
variable (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] [Algebra R B] [IsScalarTower R A B]
variable {K₁ : Type u} [AddCommGroup K₁] [Module R K₁] [Module.Finite R K₁]
  [Module.Projective R K₁]
variable {K₀ : Type u} [AddCommGroup K₀] [Module R K₀] [Module.Finite R K₀]
  [Module.Projective R K₀]

/-- **The comparison of the determinant line of a two-term complex with flat base change is
transitive.** Base changing an element `φ` of `det(K)` from `R` to `A` and then to `B` gives,
after conjugating by the determinant equivalences of the cancellations
`B ⊗_A (A ⊗_R K_i) ≅ B ⊗_R K_i`, the base change of `φ` from `R` to `B`.

The comparison is conjugation by `ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv`
(`TwoTermComplex.determinantLineBaseChange_one_tmul`), so this is
`ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv_comp_tmul` at `K₁` and at `K₀`. -/
theorem determinantLineBaseChange_comp (f : K₁ →ₗ[R] K₀) (φ : determinantLine f) :
    determinantLineBaseChange B (LinearMap.baseChange A f)
        ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[A] determinantLineBaseChange A f ((1 : A) ⊗ₜ[R] φ)) =
      (ProjectiveDeterminant.mapEquiv
          (cancelBaseChange R A B B K₀)).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ
        determinantLineBaseChange B f ((1 : B) ⊗ₜ[R] φ) ∘ₗ
          (ProjectiveDeterminant.mapEquiv (cancelBaseChange R A B B K₁)).toLinearMap := by
  simp only [determinantLineBaseChange_one_tmul]
  refine LinearMap.ext fun y => ?_
  obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := (ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv
    (R := A) (A := B) (M := A ⊗[R] K₁)).surjective y
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply]
  induction v using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
  | add v w hv hw => simp only [map_add, hv, hw]
  | tmul b z =>
      obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := (ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv
        (R := R) (A := A) (M := K₁)).surjective z
      induction u using TensorProduct.inductionOn with
      | add u u' hu hu' => simp only [map_add, TensorProduct.tmul_add, hu, hu']
      | tmul a x =>
          refine (LinearEquiv.eq_symm_apply _).mpr ?_
          rw [LinearMap.baseChange_tmul]
          simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply,
            LinearMap.baseChange_tmul]
          rw [ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv_comp_tmul,
            ProjectiveDeterminant.baseChangeEquiv_comp_tmul, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply,
            LinearMap.baseChange_tmul]

end TwoTermComplex

end
